   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">The House Committee on Overseas Workers Affairs (HCOWA) of the House of Representatives conducted two high level tripartite maritime dialogue involving the national and international maritime stakeholders, including  the International Transport Federation (ITF), International Chamber of Shipping (ICS) as well as the International Maritime Organization (IMO). The dialogue discussed more broad issues on progress made and remaining challenges as well as on the way forward on crew change in the context of COVID-19, ensuring  that Filipino seafarers can safely get on ships and get home (July 17, 2021 and August 27, 2021). The ILO participated in the preliminary discussions organized by HCOWA (June 25, 2020) to present and clarify the contents of  Briefing Note on Maritime Labour Issues and Coronavirus (COVID-19, which was also presented during the first High level Maritime Dialogue).  During the  ILO proposed the   high level dialogue between the Philippines and the international maritime stakeholders.    The ILO mobilized the international maritime stakeholders (ICS, ITF and IMO). The dialogue facilitated cooperation between the national and international maritime stakeholders. The ILO   collaborated with the HCOWA and contributed to the programme design   for the preparations for the two High Level Maritime Dialogues in 2021 and 2021.</narrative>
